<details id="table-editor-panel" class="table-editor-panel"><summary>Article tables: create or edit</summary>
<p class="small">Edit cells without writing pipe-table syntax. Choose a supported article table or create one at the article end. Preparation stays separate until you preview and apply.</p>
<label for="table-select">Table in this article</label><select id="table-select" disabled></select><p id="table-list-status" class="small"></p>
<div class="actions"><button id="table-open-selected" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Edit selected table</button><button id="table-use-cursor" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Use table at article cursor</button><button id="table-create" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>New table at article end</button></div>
<p id="table-target-status" class="small">Choose an existing table or create one.</p><button id="table-recheck" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Recheck selected table, keep prepared cells</button>
<section id="table-working" hidden aria-labelledby="table-working-heading"><h3 id="table-working-heading">Prepare table cells</h3>
<p id="table-cell-help" class="small">One line per cell, up to 2,000 characters. Simple Markdown inside cells is supported. Cell edges are trimmed and literal pipes escaped when applying a change. Headers are required for new or changed tables. Scroll the grid horizontally for wider tables.</p>
<div class="table-edit-grid" id="table-grid" role="region" aria-label="Editable table cells, scroll horizontally if needed" tabindex="0" aria-describedby="table-cell-help"></div>
<div class="actions"><button id="table-previous-page" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Previous rows</button><button id="table-next-page" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Next rows</button></div><p id="table-page-status" class="small"></p>
<div class="actions"><button id="table-add-row" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Add row at end</button><button id="table-add-column" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Add column at end</button></div>
<div class="actions"><button id="table-preview-change" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Preview table change</button><button id="table-preview-remove" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Preview removing this table</button></div></section>
<section id="table-change-preview" hidden aria-labelledby="table-change-heading"><h3 id="table-change-heading">Review the exact table change</h3><p id="table-change-summary" class="small"></p>
<details id="table-reading-panel" open><summary>Prepared table preview</summary><div id="table-reading-preview" class="article-preview" role="region" aria-label="Reading preview of the prepared table" tabindex="0"></div></details>
<details id="table-source-panel"><summary>Exact source before and after</summary><label for="table-before">Article table to replace</label><textarea id="table-before" rows="3" readonly></textarea><label for="table-after">Markdown to insert</label><textarea id="table-after" rows="4" readonly></textarea></details></section>
<div class="actions"><button id="table-apply" type="button" class="button" disabled>Apply table change</button><button id="table-discard" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Discard table preparation</button></div>
<p id="table-editor-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">Table editor is loading. You can edit table Markdown directly.</p>
<p class="small">Up to twelve columns and 100 data rows, edited ten rows at a time. No merged cells or multiline cells. Applying saves an in-tab checkpoint and clears export approval and the linked-image choice. Unsaved preparation is excluded from backups, collections, and exports. Closing clears the preview and keeps prepared cells. <a href="/help/local-workspace/#table-editor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Table editing help (new tab)</a></p>
</details>
